<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  floppy's Speaking ability: it encodes a reply's parts to speech, plays
  it out as environment.sound, and records the words in the conversation. The communication (abilities/
  communication/communication.scx) invokes it as its child "speaking" and routes each
  selected response to it. Cognition never selects it directly
  (bot.ability.speaking.input is not offered).

    idle -bot.ability.speaking.input-> speaking { voicing { encoding
      -> playing { sounding <-> starved } } -> recording } -> idle
    encoding, playing -bot.ability.speaking.stop-> recording

  voicing invokes the vocal SpeechEncoding (abilities/vocal/vocal.scx, its
  child "vocal", which invokes the speech service) and, once vocal is ready (its
  first bot.ability.offers), sends it bot.ability.vocal.speech.encoding.input
  {parts}: the input's parts (1 to 64 parts {expression?, words?},
  decision D178), whose words, joined exactly as written, are the
  utterance's text of record. Input that does not
  say something (a part with neither words, a sound nor a pause, an
  expression that directs no cue, or blank words) is refused with
  bot.ability.failed. The audio is written to output_prefix + operation + "." + the
  media subtype (a path in the media directory the run grants the speech
  service). The encoding streams (decision D203): vocal sends each
  bot.ability.vocal.speech.encoding.chunk {audio, sequence, media_type,
  sample_rate_hz, channels, duration} as the speech service encodes it
  (the audio a file of its own; media_type, sample_rate_hz and channels
  speaking's own, 24000 Hz mono audio/pcm, where the encoder leaves one
  null; duration when the encoder measured one, as the speech service
  does for linear PCM), then the whole utterance's
  bot.ability.vocal.speech.encoding.output. Vocal stays invoked while the
  chunks play, so playout starts on the first chunk, and synthesis
  (until the output) is bounded by encoding_timeout_ms, 30 s (decision
  D98, 30 s being the stage_timeout_ms of the interpretation, reading and
  seeing); leaving voicing cancels vocal and its request. An output with
  no chunk before it has nothing to play and fails the utterance.

  playing begins on the first chunk and issues the efference copy first,
  on entry (the copy leaves before the sound does):
  bot.ability.speaking.efference {mouth, duration, media_type,
  sample_rate_hz, channels} to the parent, which carries it to the bot's
  Listening; mouth is the <data> mouth, "speaking", the sound's source
  (devices are out of scope), and duration the measured audio received and
  not yet played. No copy is sent when nothing received has a duration.
  Then the words are logged as floppy.say, and each chunk in turn
  (sounding) is broadcast as it starts: environment.sound {audio,
  media_type, sample_rate_hz, channels, source} to the parent, which the
  body puts into the environment. source is the mouth (a relayed SCXML event
  keeps only its data, so the source travels in the sound): it is how the listening's sensitivity
  tells the bot's own voice from a sound that only arrives while it speaks.
  With the first chunk's sound the parent gets
  bot.ability.speaking.progress {spoken_seconds: 0}, a sign of life as the
  first audio starts. Chunks that arrive while one sounds wait their turn.

  Playout lasts as long as the audio (decision D179): a mouth plays each
  commanded piece (at most half of lookahead_ms, 1 s, and never past the
  end of its chunk) in real time and reports its mark, devices.audio.played
  {mark}; until the mouth (a device) is ported, speaking times each report
  itself with a <send delay> of the piece's length, one piece at a time,
  marks "u<operation>.<n>". Each report is followed by an efference copy of
  the audio received and still to play and bot.ability.speaking.progress
  {spoken_seconds} (the seconds reported played), which re-arms the
  communication's response timer. After a chunk's last piece the next
  chunk sounds; when it was the utterance's last (the output has arrived)
  the progress is followed by the copy {duration: 0}, which closes the
  listening's window; and when the next has not arrived yet the progress
  alone is sent and playing waits (starved) for it, its copy leaving
  before its sound, or for the output, whose copy is {duration: 0}. A
  chunk with no measured duration has no pieces and counts as played at
  once. A vocal failure, the encoding timer or an error mid-stream sends
  the copy {duration: 0} (the mouth stops) and answers bot.ability.failed.

  Stop: bot.ability.speaking.stop {} names no utterance: it stops the one
  in hand, since an SCXML <send> takes no id from an expression, so the
  communication cannot name its response's id on it (decision D179). In
  encoding it cancels vocal and its request; in playing it cancels the
  next mark and, mid-stream, the encoding still under way (leaving
  voicing cancels vocal). Either way the efference copy {duration: 0}
  leaves at once (nothing more is commanded, so the listening's window
  closes) and the utterance is recorded with outcome "stopped". What was
  said is what the reported marks cover: the words in proportion to the
  share of the audio played, rounded down to whole words, the audio being
  what was received while the encoding still streamed (decision D203); a
  piece cut short counts as unplayed (no mouth reports how much of it
  played). The chunks already in the environment stay there (the
  environment has no flush); the chunks not yet sounding never go in. A
  stop in idle or in recording has nothing to stop and is logged
  (speaking.stale).

  recording builds the outbound message with <conversation:message_for_turn>
  (direction outbound, content what was spoken, content_type text/plain,
  and participants the bot's own voice stamped own, which it has none of
  until it is voiced, decision D176) and sends
  bot.ability.conversation.append {message} to the parent, which holds the
  conversation (a sibling is out of a child's reach: SCXML sends go only to
  #_parent and to a session's own children); an utterance that spoke
  nothing records nothing (decision D179). It is bounded by 5 s
  (recording_timeout_ms). Then it answers the parent with
  bot.ability.speaking.output {text, spoken, unspoken, outcome, voice_id,
  media_type, sample_rate_hz, channels} (decision D179: text the words
  asked for, spoken what the played audio covers, unspoken the rest,
  outcome "completed" or "stopped"; voice_id is null, as the bot has no
  voice of its own until persona voices it, parity decision 6; no per-part
  expression is reported, as no encoder applies a cue, D178).

  Failures: a vocal failure (its bot.ability.failed), an encoding or
  recording timeout, or a vocal that cannot run answers the parent with
  bot.ability.failed {message} (the terminal failure) and returns to idle.
  Timers are bot.ability.speaking.apply.failed {message} sends (speaking's
  own failure event), taken only by the timer in hand (_event.sendid).

  Utterances: an utterance's id is its input's sendid (none when the
  sender named none). Leaving speaking retires it into the last
  finished_utterances_bound (16) ids, and an input for a finished id, or
  another copy of the one in hand or of a held one (held_ids), is dropped
  and logged (speaking.late).
  Input for another utterance that arrives while one is in hand is held by
  <event:defer/> (scxml.rs namespaces/event), up to held_utterances_bound
  (16), and past that is refused with bot.ability.failed (decision D175);
  held input is taken, in order, on the return to idle.

  Contracts: the input's contract is schemas/bot.ability.speaking.input.json:
  a send whose data it rejects is never routed here and raises
  error.execution in the sender (scxml.rs session.accepts-event-data).
  vocal's events are checked where vocal creates them.

  Readiness: every entry into idle sends bot.ability.offers {ability:
  "speaking", choices: []} to the parent; it offers nothing.

  Bindings: the conversation namespace package; vocal's speech service.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:conversation="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/conversation"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="speaking" initial="idle">
  <datamodel>
    <!-- Configuration: defaults and bounds. -->
    <data id="sample_rate_hz" expr="24000"/>
    <data id="channels" expr="1"/>
    <data id="media_type" expr="'audio/pcm'"/>
    <!-- The speech provider, model and voice vocal asks the speech
         service for (Gemini by default). -->
    <data id="provider" expr="'gemini'"/>
    <data id="model" expr="'gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview'"/>
    <data id="voice" expr="'Kore'"/>
    <data id="output_prefix" expr="'media/speaking-'"/>
    <!-- The mouth: the efference copy's mouth and the sound's source, so
         the listening can tell its own voice apart. -->
    <data id="mouth" expr="'speaking'"/>
    <data id="encoding_timeout_ms" expr="30000"/>
    <data id="recording_timeout_ms" expr="5000"/>
    <!-- The most unplayed audio commanded ahead of the mouth: a piece is
         at most half of it (decision D179). -->
    <data id="lookahead_ms" expr="1000"/>
    <!-- The utterance in hand, its number, id (its input's sendid, null
         when the sender named none), the encoded speech and timer. -->
    <data id="operation" expr="0"/>
    <data id="utterance_id" expr="null"/>
    <data id="parts" expr="null"/>
    <data id="text" expr="null"/>
    <data id="encoded" expr="null"/>
    <data id="message" expr="null"/>
    <data id="timer" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The playout in hand (decision D203): the chunks received and not
         yet sounding, the chunk sounding, whether the whole utterance is
         encoded, the measured audio received and what of it (and of the
         chunk in hand) the mouth reported played, in ms, the piece being
         reported, how many chunks sounded and pieces were commanded, the
         pending mark (its send id), and how the utterance ends and what
         it said. -->
    <data id="chunks" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="chunk" expr="null"/>
    <data id="encoded_all" expr="false"/>
    <data id="received_ms" expr="0"/>
    <data id="played_ms" expr="0"/>
    <data id="chunk_played_ms" expr="0"/>
    <data id="piece_ms" expr="0"/>
    <data id="sounds" expr="0"/>
    <data id="commands" expr="0"/>
    <data id="mark" expr="null"/>
    <data id="outcome" expr="null"/>
    <data id="spoken" expr="null"/>
    <data id="unspoken" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The ids of the last finished_utterances_bound utterances said, so a
         late copy of one never reopens it, and how many other utterances
         wait while one is said (decision D175). -->
    <data id="finished_utterances_bound" expr="16"/>
    <data id="finished_utterances" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="held_utterances_bound" expr="16"/>
    <data id="held" expr="0"/>
    <data id="held_ids" expr="[]"/>
  </datamodel>
  <script src="speaking.js"/>

  <state id="idle">
    <onentry>
      <send event="bot.ability.offers" target="#_parent">
        <param name="ability" expr="'speaking'"/>
        <param name="choices" expr="[]"/>
      </send>
    </onentry>
    <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.speaking.input.json"
                cond="isFinishedUtterance(_event)">
      <log label="speaking.late" expr="_event.sendid"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- A reply that says nothing is refused before it is an utterance
         (decision D178). -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.speaking.input.json"
                cond="isUnspokenInput(_event)" target="idle">
      <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
        <param name="message" expr="'A reply must say something: every part needs words, a sound or a pause, and the words must not be blank.'"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.speaking.input.json"
                target="encoding">
      <assign location="parts" expr="_event.data.parts"/>
      <assign location="text" expr="said(parts)"/>
      <assign location="utterance_id" expr="utteranceId(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- Nothing in hand to stop. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.stop" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.speaking.stop.json">
      <log label="speaking.stale" expr="_event.name"/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <!-- One utterance in hand, from its encoding to its record; other input
       is held throughout, and leaving releases it (decision D175). -->
  <state id="speaking" initial="voicing">
    <onentry>
      <assign location="encoded" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="encoded_all" expr="false"/>
      <assign location="chunks" expr="[]"/>
      <assign location="chunk" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="received_ms" expr="0"/>
      <assign location="played_ms" expr="0"/>
      <assign location="chunk_played_ms" expr="0"/>
      <assign location="sounds" expr="0"/>
      <assign location="commands" expr="0"/>
      <assign location="mark" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="outcome" expr="'completed'"/>
    </onentry>
    <onexit>
      <assign location="finished_utterances" expr="finishedUtterances()"/>
      <assign location="utterance_id" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="held" expr="0"/>
      <assign location="held_ids" expr="[]"/>
    </onexit>
    <!-- A late copy of a finished utterance, or another copy of this one or
         of a held one, is dropped; another utterance waits its turn, up to
         held_utterances_bound, and past that is refused (decision D175). -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.speaking.input.json"
                cond="isLateUtterance(_event)">
      <log label="speaking.late" expr="_event.sendid"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.speaking.input.json"
                cond="canHold()">
      <event:defer/>
      <assign location="held" expr="held + 1"/>
      <assign location="held_ids" expr="heldIds(_event)"/>
      <log label="speaking.deferred" expr="_event.name"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.speaking.input.json">
      <log label="speaking.rejected" expr="heldOverMessage()"/>
      <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
        <param name="message" expr="'Speaking is holding too many utterances; this one is refused.'"/>
      </send>
    </transition>

    <!-- The vocal encodes while the chunks it has sent play out: leaving
         voicing cancels it, its request with it. -->
    <state id="voicing" initial="encoding">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="operation" expr="nextOperation()"/>
        <send idlocation="timer" event="bot.ability.speaking.apply.failed" delayexpr="delay(encoding_timeout_ms)">
          <param name="message" expr="'Speech encoding timed out.'"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendidexpr="timer"/>
      </onexit>
      <invoke id="vocal" type="scxml" src="../vocal/vocal.scx">
        <param name="output" expr="outputPath()"/>
        <param name="provider" expr="provider"/>
        <param name="model" expr="model"/>
        <param name="voice" expr="voice"/>
        <param name="media_type" expr="media_type"/>
      </invoke>

      <!-- Synthesis: no sound exists yet. -->
      <state id="encoding">
        <transition event="bot.ability.offers" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.offers.json">
          <send event="bot.ability.vocal.speech.encoding.input" target="#_vocal">
            <param name="parts" expr="parts"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <!-- The first chunk: the sound starts. -->
        <transition event="bot.ability.vocal.speech.encoding.chunk" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.vocal.speech.encoding.chunk.json"
                    target="playing">
          <assign location="encoded" expr="chunkFormat(_event)"/>
          <assign location="chunks" expr="queued(_event)"/>
          <assign location="received_ms" expr="received_ms + chunkMs(_event)"/>
        </transition>
        <!-- An encoding that ends without a chunk has nothing to play. -->
        <transition event="bot.ability.vocal.speech.encoding.output" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.vocal.speech.encoding.output.json" target="idle">
          <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
            <param name="message" expr="'Speech encoding answered no audio.'"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="idle">
          <assign location="message" expr="_event.data.message"/>
          <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
            <param name="message" expr="message"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.apply.failed" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.speaking.apply.failed.json"
                    cond="isTimer(_event)" target="idle">
          <log label="speaking.timed_out" expr="encodingTimedOutLog()"/>
          <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
            <param name="message" expr="_event.data.message"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition event="error.* done.invoke.vocal" target="idle">
          <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
            <param name="message" expr="encodingRunFailure(_event)"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <!-- Stopped before any sound: nothing was said. -->
        <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.stop" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.speaking.stop.json" target="recording">
          <assign location="outcome" expr="'stopped'"/>
          <assign location="spoken" expr="''"/>
          <assign location="unspoken" expr="text"/>
          <send event="bot.ability.speaking.efference" target="#_parent">
            <content expr="efferenceCopy(0)"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- Playout, chunk by chunk as they arrive: the copy leaves before
           the sound does, and each chunk lasts as long as its audio, piece
           by piece. -->
      <state id="playing" initial="sounding">
        <onentry>
          <if cond="hasDuration()">
            <send event="bot.ability.speaking.efference" target="#_parent">
              <content expr="efferenceCopy(remainingSeconds())"/>
            </send>
          </if>
          <log label="floppy.say" expr="text"/>
        </onentry>
        <!-- More of the utterance: queued behind the chunk in hand. -->
        <transition event="bot.ability.vocal.speech.encoding.chunk" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.vocal.speech.encoding.chunk.json">
          <assign location="chunks" expr="queued(_event)"/>
          <assign location="received_ms" expr="received_ms + chunkMs(_event)"/>
        </transition>
        <!-- The whole utterance is encoded: no more chunks, and no more
             encoding bound. -->
        <transition event="bot.ability.vocal.speech.encoding.output" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.vocal.speech.encoding.output.json">
          <assign location="encoded_all" expr="true"/>
          <assign location="encoded" expr="encodedFormat(_event)"/>
          <cancel sendidexpr="timer"/>
        </transition>
        <!-- The encoding failed or ran out of time mid-stream: the mouth
             stops, so the copy says nothing is left. -->
        <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="idle">
          <send event="bot.ability.speaking.efference" target="#_parent">
            <content expr="efferenceCopy(0)"/>
          </send>
          <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
            <param name="message" expr="_event.data.message"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.apply.failed" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.speaking.apply.failed.json"
                    cond="isTimer(_event)" target="idle">
          <log label="speaking.timed_out" expr="encodingTimedOutLog()"/>
          <send event="bot.ability.speaking.efference" target="#_parent">
            <content expr="efferenceCopy(0)"/>
          </send>
          <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
            <param name="message" expr="_event.data.message"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition event="error.* done.invoke.vocal" target="idle">
          <send event="bot.ability.speaking.efference" target="#_parent">
            <content expr="efferenceCopy(0)"/>
          </send>
          <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
            <param name="message" expr="playoutFailure(_event)"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <!-- Stopped: nothing more plays, and the encoding is cancelled;
             what was said is what the reported pieces cover. -->
        <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.stop" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.speaking.stop.json" target="recording">
          <assign location="outcome" expr="'stopped'"/>
          <assign location="spoken" expr="spokenWords()"/>
          <assign location="unspoken" expr="text.slice(spoken.length)"/>
          <send event="bot.ability.speaking.efference" target="#_parent">
            <content expr="efferenceCopy(0)"/>
          </send>
        </transition>

        <!-- One chunk in hand: its sound goes into the environment, and
             the mouth plays it piece by piece. -->
        <state id="sounding">
          <onentry>
            <assign location="chunk" expr="chunks[0]"/>
            <assign location="chunks" expr="chunks.slice(1)"/>
            <assign location="chunk_played_ms" expr="0"/>
            <send event="environment.sound" target="#_parent">
              <param name="audio" expr="chunk.audio"/>
              <param name="media_type" expr="chunk.media_type"/>
              <param name="sample_rate_hz" expr="chunk.sample_rate_hz"/>
              <param name="channels" expr="chunk.channels"/>
              <param name="source" expr="mouth"/>
            </send>
            <if cond="isFirstSound()">
              <send event="bot.ability.speaking.progress" target="#_parent">
                <param name="spoken_seconds" expr="0"/>
              </send>
            </if>
            <assign location="sounds" expr="sounds + 1"/>
            <if cond="chunkHasDuration()">
              <send idlocation="mark" event="devices.audio.played" delayexpr="delay(nextPieceMs())">
                <param name="mark" expr="markName()"/>
              </send>
              <assign location="commands" expr="commands + 1"/>
            <else/>
              <raise event="bot.ability.speaking.apply.completed"/>
            </if>
          </onentry>
          <onexit>
            <if cond="hasMark()">
              <cancel sendidexpr="mark"/>
            </if>
          </onexit>
          <!-- The mouth reported the chunk's last piece played: the next
               chunk, the end of the utterance, or a wait for more. -->
          <transition event="devices.audio.played" event:schema="../schemas/devices.audio.played.json"
                      cond="endsChunkWithMore(_event)" target="sounding">
            <assign location="played_ms" expr="played_ms + nextPieceMs()"/>
            <send event="bot.ability.speaking.efference" target="#_parent">
              <content expr="efferenceCopy(remainingSeconds())"/>
            </send>
            <send event="bot.ability.speaking.progress" target="#_parent">
              <param name="spoken_seconds" expr="played_ms / 1000"/>
            </send>
          </transition>
          <transition event="devices.audio.played" event:schema="../schemas/devices.audio.played.json"
                      cond="endsUtterance(_event)" target="recording">
            <assign location="played_ms" expr="played_ms + nextPieceMs()"/>
            <assign location="spoken" expr="text"/>
            <assign location="unspoken" expr="''"/>
            <send event="bot.ability.speaking.progress" target="#_parent">
              <param name="spoken_seconds" expr="played_ms / 1000"/>
            </send>
            <send event="bot.ability.speaking.efference" target="#_parent">
              <content expr="efferenceCopy(0)"/>
            </send>
          </transition>
          <transition event="devices.audio.played" event:schema="../schemas/devices.audio.played.json"
                      cond="endsChunk(_event)" target="starved">
            <assign location="played_ms" expr="played_ms + nextPieceMs()"/>
            <send event="bot.ability.speaking.progress" target="#_parent">
              <param name="spoken_seconds" expr="played_ms / 1000"/>
            </send>
          </transition>
          <!-- A piece within the chunk: the copy of what is still to come,
               the progress, and the next piece. -->
          <transition event="devices.audio.played" event:schema="../schemas/devices.audio.played.json"
                      cond="isMark(_event)" type="internal">
            <assign location="piece_ms" expr="nextPieceMs()"/>
            <assign location="played_ms" expr="played_ms + piece_ms"/>
            <assign location="chunk_played_ms" expr="chunk_played_ms + piece_ms"/>
            <send event="bot.ability.speaking.efference" target="#_parent">
              <content expr="efferenceCopy(remainingSeconds())"/>
            </send>
            <send event="bot.ability.speaking.progress" target="#_parent">
              <param name="spoken_seconds" expr="played_ms / 1000"/>
            </send>
            <send idlocation="mark" event="devices.audio.played" delayexpr="delay(nextPieceMs())">
              <param name="mark" expr="markName()"/>
            </send>
            <assign location="commands" expr="commands + 1"/>
          </transition>
          <!-- A chunk with no measured duration counts as played at once. -->
          <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.apply.completed" cond="hasQueued()" target="sounding"/>
          <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.apply.completed" cond="encoded_all" target="recording">
            <assign location="spoken" expr="text"/>
            <assign location="unspoken" expr="''"/>
            <if cond="hasDuration()">
              <send event="bot.ability.speaking.efference" target="#_parent">
                <content expr="efferenceCopy(0)"/>
              </send>
            </if>
          </transition>
          <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.apply.completed" target="starved"/>
        </state>

        <!-- Everything received has played: waiting for the next chunk or
             the end of the encoding (still bounded by encoding_timeout_ms). -->
        <state id="starved">
          <transition event="bot.ability.vocal.speech.encoding.chunk" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.vocal.speech.encoding.chunk.json"
                      target="sounding">
            <assign location="chunks" expr="queued(_event)"/>
            <assign location="received_ms" expr="received_ms + chunkMs(_event)"/>
            <if cond="hasRemaining()">
              <send event="bot.ability.speaking.efference" target="#_parent">
                <content expr="efferenceCopy(remainingSeconds())"/>
              </send>
            </if>
          </transition>
          <transition event="bot.ability.vocal.speech.encoding.output" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.vocal.speech.encoding.output.json"
                      target="recording">
            <assign location="encoded_all" expr="true"/>
            <assign location="encoded" expr="encodedFormat(_event)"/>
            <assign location="spoken" expr="text"/>
            <assign location="unspoken" expr="''"/>
            <if cond="hasDuration()">
              <send event="bot.ability.speaking.efference" target="#_parent">
                <content expr="efferenceCopy(0)"/>
              </send>
            </if>
          </transition>
        </state>
      </state>
    </state>

    <!-- The words go into the conversation's exchange. -->
    <state id="recording">
      <onentry>
        <send idlocation="timer" event="bot.ability.speaking.apply.failed" delayexpr="delay(recording_timeout_ms)">
          <param name="message" expr="'Conversation history recording timed out.'"/>
        </send>
        <if cond="hasSpoken()">
          <conversation:message_for_turn location="message" direction="outbound" event="'bot.ability.conversation.append'"
                                         message="outboundMessage()" provenance="({id: 'speaking-' + operation})"/>
          <send event="bot.ability.conversation.append" target="#_parent">
            <param name="message" expr="message"/>
          </send>
        </if>
        <raise event="bot.ability.speaking.conversation.recorded"/>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendidexpr="timer"/>
      </onexit>
      <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.conversation.recorded" target="idle">
        <send event="bot.ability.speaking.output" target="#_parent">
          <content expr="speechProduct()"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.apply.failed" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.speaking.apply.failed.json"
                  cond="isTimer(_event)" target="idle">
        <log label="speaking.timed_out" expr="recordingTimedOutLog()"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
          <param name="message" expr="_event.data.message"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="error.*" target="idle">
        <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
          <param name="message" expr="recordingFailure(_event)"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <!-- Played out already: nothing left to stop. -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.stop" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.speaking.stop.json">
        <log label="speaking.stale" expr="_event.name"/>
      </transition>
    </state>
  </state>
</scxml>
